meta {
  name: Delete Cluster
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/clusters/{{clusterId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
}

docs {
  Removes a cluster record. Requires ClusterAdmin (own org) or PlatformAdmin.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Authentication required.
    2. Parse cluster ID — 404 if not a valid UUID or not found.
    3. ClusterAdmin may only delete clusters owned by their own org; PlatformAdmin may delete any.
    4. Refuse if any non-terminal deployments (state not in deleted/failed_*) exist on the cluster.
    5. Hard-delete the cluster row.
    6. Write cluster.deleted to audit_logs.

  Responses:
    204 No Content         — deleted
    401 unauthorized       — unauthenticated
    403 forbidden          — ClusterAdmin trying to delete outside their org
    404 not_found          — cluster not found
    409 active_deployments_blocking — drain deployments first
}
